_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["2 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","vague/subjective terms present: as needed"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add integration cases for invalid/empty inputs: an unresolvable checkpoint commit, a retired_path with no introducing commit, and an absent remote-tracking tickets ref — asserting the documented disposition for each.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'covering old-reachable, recent-reachable, and old-unreachable cases for both checkpoint commits and .retired tombstones'","ABSENCE: no case for an unresolvable commit, a retired_path never introduced by any commit, or a missing refs/remotes/<sync.remote>/<tracker.branch>."],"finding":"The testing plan covers old-reachable, recent-reachable, and old-unreachable for both target forms, but does not cover invalid/empty-input boundaries: a checkpoint commit that does not resolve, a `.retired` path with no introducing commit in history, or the configured remote-tracking ref being entirely absent locally. These are the predicate's non-happy inputs that determine whether it fails safely or throws.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f13e54f4d2de43f67","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing section ('RED first' integration cases)","norm_id":"ncf3201ecf9e22051","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the disposition of each non-happy git-read arm: what the predicate returns/raises when the configured remote-tracking ref is absent locally, when the checkpoint commit or retired path does not resolve, and when a git subcommand errors (and distinguish 'ref absent' from 'commit not reachable from an existing ref').","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.failure-disposition-contract","T5b"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8263,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'checks the corresponding remote-tracking tickets ref, and returns true only when the checkpoint commit is an ancestor of that ref'","'All git operations are read-only ... against the current local view of the configured sync remote's tickets ref.'","ABSENCE: no statement of what surfaces when the ref is missing, when a commit/path fails to resolve, or when a git subcommand errors — distinct from the AC's 'not reachable from an existing ref' case."],"finding":"The plan explicitly never fetches and reads only the 'current local view' of refs/remotes/<sync.remote>/<tracker.branch>, but does not state what the predicate does when that remote-tracking ref is absent locally (the normal state before any fetch), when the checkpoint commit does not resolve, or when merge-base/rev-parse exits with an error rather than a clean ancestor/not-ancestor result. It is unstated whether these surface as a false result or an exception, and with what disposition.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f844a539e30e4ce91","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Implementation plan step 1 & 4 ('the corresponding remote-tracking tickets ref' / 'against the current local view')","norm_id":"n679a810187b727bd","priority":0.1237,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a 'Failure-disposition contract' note: e.g. an absent remote-tracking ref returns false-but-surfaces a distinct signal/log (fatal/permanent config-or-fetch problem, not a silent not-eligible), an unresolvable commit/path is a permanent error surfaced to the caller, and only a resolvable-but-not-ancestor commit returns the ordinary false verdict.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Reconcile the age computation with ADR 0106 C3's 'reachable-for-N-days' semantics: either justify in-plan why the checkpoint's committer timestamp is a sound proxy for remote-reachability duration (e.g. the S1 collapse engine stamps the checkpoint committer-date to its actual publish time), or measure reachability age from a remote-ref backup/reflog observation rather than the commit's own committer-date.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan step 1: 'returns true only when the checkpoint commit is an ancestor of that ref and the checkpoint commit's committer timestamp is at least [reclaim].horizon_days old'","ADR 0106 C3: 'The collapse checkpoint has been reachable from the sync-remote tickets ref for >= N days ... This is the guarantee that no reachable-elsewhere object is dropped.'","ADR 0106 §3.3: the checkpoint is created via `git commit-tree boundary^{tree}` — a newly-minted commit whose committer-date is set at creation, not derived from remote-reachability duration","ABSENCE: the plan proposes only rev-parse/merge-base/show/log, none of which measure how long an object has been reachable from a ref; git records no such timestamp"],"finding":"The plan's eligibility mechanism substitutes the checkpoint commit's committer timestamp for the ADR 0106 C3 quantity 'reachable from the sync-remote tickets ref for >= N days', but these are not equivalent — committer-date does not measure remote-reachability duration, and a freshly published checkpoint (created via git commit-tree per ADR 0106 §3) can carry a backdated committer timestamp that passes the horizon with zero days of actual remote reachability.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f73c5ea047a637cab","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Implementation plan step 1 / AC lines 1-2 ('the checkpoint commit's committer timestamp is at least [reclaim].horizon_days old')","norm_id":"nb75cf345275d71b3","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A checkpoint commit is created and pushed today but carries a backdated committer timestamp (e.g. inherited/stamped >= N days ago); the ancestor check passes and the age check passes, so eligibility returns true on day 0 — before any clone has had N days to converge, violating C3 and risking dropping objects an unconverged clone still needs.","A checkpoint that has genuinely been remote-reachable for > N days but was authored with a recent committer-date is wrongly judged ineligible."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Add a one- or two-sentence positive rationale stating why the checkpoint's committer timestamp is the correct/safe age basis for the C3 horizon (and under what S1-engine invariant it equals actual remote-reachability age).","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan step 1 and step 4 describe WHAT git commands are read-only but never state WHY committer-date is an adequate stand-in for 'reachable from the remote ref for >= N days'","ABSENCE: no sentence in the plan connects the committer-timestamp choice to the C3 convergence guarantee or explains its safety"],"finding":"The plan states no positive rationale for choosing the checkpoint's committer timestamp as the age basis over the remote-reachability duration that ADR 0106 C3 actually names; the reader cannot tell whether the proxy is intentional and safe.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1165857f50a7ac56","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Implementation plan step 1","norm_id":"nf00863775c024d5e","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer or reviewer cannot verify the horizon computation is faithful to C3 because the design decision (committer-date as reachability-age proxy) is unexplained."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"1fcf456fcab61da4","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["adbae38274cc8a86",4012],"description_boxes":["8b6fa01313ce51af",0],"file_impact":["d0c7bdf075b6942d",10],"ticket_id":["158a6998d1200c18",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":427102,"cache_write_tokens":213451,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms":4204.2,"input_tokens":665255,"llm_calls":28,"llm_ms":178528.2,"output_tokens":22817,"precheck":{"cited_anchor_warning":false},"total_ms":214740.1,"verify_requests":10},"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","priority_floor":0.8,"provider_provenance":{"candidates":["bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-